Part A: Cheer-Goldston class LP (RH side), Lam=2.5, grid 0.01, positivity to u=60
  P = rhat(0) + 2 int_0^1 a rhat = 1.3209166550   simple proportion 2-P = 0.6790833450   (CGdL 2020: 1.3208 / 0.6792)
  Montgomery-Taylor value for comparison: 1/2 + 2^(-1/2) cot(2^(-1/2)) = 1.3274992963 -> 0.6725007037
  R = int_{-1}^1 rho = 1.01261107 ; kappa = r(0) = 1 ; min rhat on [0,1] = 0.000e+00 (rho >= 0 inside) ; min rhat on (1,Lam] = -0.02019
  r_in = bandwidth-one part: min r_in(u) = -0.004744 at u = 2.100 ; completion mass s(0) = R - 1 = 0.012611
  NUMERICAL: LP with grid positivity; not an exact certificate of r >= 0 (the RH-side value is CGdL's theorem).

